{
  "mn66:0.1": "Middle Discourses 66 ",
  "mn66:0.2": "The Simile of the Quail ",
  "mn66:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn66:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Aṅguttarāpans, near the town of theirs named Āpaṇa. ",
  "mn66:2.1": "Then the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Āpaṇa for alms. ",
  "mn66:2.2": "He wandered for alms in Āpaṇa. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to a certain forest grove for the day’s meditation. ",
  "mn66:2.3": "Having plunged deep into it, he sat at the root of a certain tree to meditate. ",
  "mn66:3.1": "Venerable Udāyī also robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Āpaṇa for alms. ",
  "mn66:3.2": "He wandered for alms in Āpaṇa. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to that forest grove for the day’s meditation. ",
  "mn66:3.3": "Having plunged deep into it, he sat at the root of a certain tree to meditate. ",
  "mn66:3.4": "Then as Venerable Udāyī was in private retreat this thought came to his mind: ",
  "mn66:4.1": "“The Buddha has rid us of so many things that bring suffering and gifted us so many things that bring happiness! ",
  "mn66:4.2": "He has rid us of so many unskillful things and gifted us so many skillful things!” ",
  "mn66:5.1": "Then in the late afternoon, Udāyī came out of retreat and went to the Buddha. He bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "mn66:6.1": "“Just now, sir, as I was in private retrea